<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<mxfile host="blueprint studio" modified="2026-10-25T19:41:24.876Z" type="device"><diagram id="recommended" name="Recommended design"><mxGraphModel grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="0" pageScale="1" math="0" shadow="0"><root><mxCell id="recommended-root"/><mxCell id="recommended-layer" parent="recommended-root"/><UserObject id="recommended-start" label="&lt;b&gt;1. You start it&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px&quot;&gt;Trigger · In Claude&lt;/font&gt;" tooltip="What happens: You hand the task over when you need it. Nothing runs on its own.&#10;&#10;Why it's here: You said you'll start it yourself.&#10;&#10;Passes on: The new item, plus any context the next step needs." step="1" kind="Start" name="You start it" runs-in="In Claude" model-or-method="Manual start" how-it-works="Runs only when a person starts it." what-happens="You hand the task over when you need it. Nothing runs on its own." why-its-here="You said you'll start it yourself." what-it-passes-on="The new item, plus any context the next step needs." next="step 2, Sort by type" rules="TL3: if A judgement task you start yourself, with no limits on AI providers, then Use Claude in the chat or desktop app, guided by a Skill."><mxCell style="rounded=1;arcSize=50;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#13201b;spacing=8;fillColor=#1c6650;strokeColor=#1c6650;fontColor=#ffffff;" vertex="1" parent="recommended-layer"><mxGeometry x="50" y="330" width="200" height="110" as="geometry"/></mxCell></UserObject><UserObject id="recommended-router" label="&lt;b&gt;2. Sort by type&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px&quot;&gt;Decision · Small, fast model · Sonnet 5.5&lt;/font&gt;" tooltip="What happens: A quick AI step reads each item and decides which type it is, so it can go down the right path.&#10;&#10;Why it's here: You said the work arrives in a few distinct types. Sorting first lets each type get its own simpler instructions and tools.&#10;&#10;Passes on: The item, labelled with its type, to that type's path." step="2" kind="Decision" name="Sort by type" runs-in="Small, fast model" model-or-method="Claude Sonnet 5.5" why-this-model="Sorting is a simple classification. A fast, balanced model is enough; a smaller one can be tested later." how-to-start="Build the first version on Claude Opus 5.5. Switch to Claude Sonnet 5.5 once it matches that baseline on your test examples. If Claude Opus 5.5 itself falls short on the hardest steps, try Claude Fable 5.1; it requires Anthropic to keep data for 30 days, so it is unavailable under zero data retention." alternative="Open-weight alternative: for example a smaller model from the same open families, chosen by testing." what-happens="A quick AI step reads each item and decides which type it is, so it can go down the right path." why-its-here="You said the work arrives in a few distinct types. Sorting first lets each type get its own simpler instructions and tools." what-it-passes-on="The item, labelled with its type, to that type's path." next="step 3, Most common type&#10;step 4, Other known types&#10;not sure: step 5, Unclear items" rules="T3: if AI workflow, and the work arrives in distinct types, then Start with routing: sort each item by type, then send it down its own path.&#10;M7: if The work is sorted by type first, then Use a small, fast model for the sorting step."><mxCell style="rhombus;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#13201b;spacing=8;fillColor=#fff6d6;strokeColor=#cfa52c;" vertex="1" parent="recommended-layer"><mxGeometry x="350" y="320" width="220" height="130" as="geometry"/></mxCell></UserObject><UserObject id="recommended-typeA" label="&lt;b&gt;3. Most common type&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px&quot;&gt;AI · Claude with your Skill · Sonnet 5.5&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px&quot;&gt;⛔ Checked against checklist&lt;/font&gt;" tooltip="What happens: This path has its own instructions and tools for the most frequent type of request. It follows the steps in your Skill. It draws on your reference library rather than guessing.&#10;&#10;Why it's here: Instructions written for one type are simpler and more reliable than one set that tries to cover everything.&#10;&#10;Passes on: A finished draft for this type." step="3" kind="AI step" name="Most common type" runs-in="Claude with your Skill" model-or-method="Claude Sonnet 5.5" why-this-model="A balanced model handles most judgement steps well at a reasonable cost per run." how-to-start="Build the first version on Claude Opus 5.5. Switch to Claude Sonnet 5.5 once it matches that baseline on your test examples. If Claude Opus 5.5 itself falls short on the hardest steps, try Claude Fable 5.1; it requires Anthropic to keep data for 30 days, so it is unavailable under zero data retention." alternative="Open-weight alternative: for example Kimi K2.6, GLM-5 or DeepSeek-V4-Pro (leading open-weight models in October 2026)." what-happens="This path has its own instructions and tools for the most frequent type of request. It follows the steps in your Skill. It draws on your reference library rather than guessing." why-its-here="Instructions written for one type are simpler and more reliable than one set that tries to cover everything." what-it-passes-on="A finished draft for this type." safeguards="Stop rule: Checked against checklist" next="step 6, You approve each result" rules="T3: if AI workflow, and the work arrives in distinct types, then Start with routing: sort each item by type, then send it down its own path.&#10;T11: if AI is used and a good result can be described as a clear checklist, then Add a generator and checker step: a second pass checks the work against your checklist and sends it back if it fails."><mxCell style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#13201b;spacing=8;fillColor=#fdebd2;strokeColor=#e0802a;strokeWidth=2;" vertex="1" parent="recommended-layer"><mxGeometry x="670" y="160" width="200" height="110" as="geometry"/></mxCell></UserObject><UserObject id="recommended-typeB" label="&lt;b&gt;4. Other known types&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px&quot;&gt;AI · Claude with your Skill · Sonnet 5.5&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px&quot;&gt;⛔ Checked against checklist&lt;/font&gt;" tooltip="What happens: Each other known type gets its own path like this one, with instructions tuned to it. It draws on your reference library rather than guessing.&#10;&#10;Why it's here: Separate paths can be tested and improved one at a time.&#10;&#10;Passes on: A finished draft for this type." step="4" kind="AI step" name="Other known types" runs-in="Claude with your Skill" model-or-method="Claude Sonnet 5.5" why-this-model="A balanced model handles most judgement steps well at a reasonable cost per run." how-to-start="Build the first version on Claude Opus 5.5. Switch to Claude Sonnet 5.5 once it matches that baseline on your test examples. If Claude Opus 5.5 itself falls short on the hardest steps, try Claude Fable 5.1; it requires Anthropic to keep data for 30 days, so it is unavailable under zero data retention." alternative="Open-weight alternative: for example Kimi K2.6, GLM-5 or DeepSeek-V4-Pro (leading open-weight models in October 2026)." what-happens="Each other known type gets its own path like this one, with instructions tuned to it. It draws on your reference library rather than guessing." why-its-here="Separate paths can be tested and improved one at a time." what-it-passes-on="A finished draft for this type." safeguards="Stop rule: Checked against checklist" next="step 6, You approve each result" rules="T3: if AI workflow, and the work arrives in distinct types, then Start with routing: sort each item by type, then send it down its own path."><mxCell style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#13201b;spacing=8;fillColor=#fdebd2;strokeColor=#e0802a;strokeWidth=2;" vertex="1" parent="recommended-layer"><mxGeometry x="670" y="330" width="200" height="110" as="geometry"/></mxCell></UserObject><UserObject id="recommended-unclear" label="&lt;b&gt;5. Unclear items&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px&quot;&gt;Person · Sent to a person&lt;/font&gt;" tooltip="What happens: Anything the sorting step isn't confident about goes straight to a person instead of being guessed.&#10;&#10;Why it's here: Misrouted items are the most common failure in this pattern. A safe default path prevents it.&#10;&#10;Passes on: The person's answer, straight to the finish." step="5" kind="Person" name="Unclear items" runs-in="Sent to a person" what-happens="Anything the sorting step isn't confident about goes straight to a person instead of being guessed." why-its-here="Misrouted items are the most common failure in this pattern. A safe default path prevents it." what-it-passes-on="The person's answer, straight to the finish." next="step 7, Result is ready" rules="T3: if AI workflow, and the work arrives in distinct types, then Start with routing: sort each item by type, then send it down its own path."><mxCell style="shape=parallelogram;perimeter=parallelogramPerimeter;fixedSize=1;size=16;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#13201b;spacing=8;fillColor=#fde4e1;strokeColor=#cf4a42;strokeWidth=2;dashed=1;" vertex="1" parent="recommended-layer"><mxGeometry x="670" y="500" width="200" height="110" as="geometry"/></mxCell></UserObject><UserObject id="recommended-approve" label="&lt;b&gt;6. You approve each result&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px&quot;&gt;Person · Before anything goes out&lt;/font&gt;" tooltip="What happens: A named person reviews every result with the checklist beside the source material and any item marked insufficient evidence, one case at a time, and approves it, changes it or sends it back. No batch approval.&#10;&#10;Why it's here: Autonomy starts at level 2. You explicitly require approval before release or action. High volume does not waive that requirement.&#10;&#10;Passes on: Approved results only. Rejected ones go back with a note, and become test examples." step="6" kind="Person" name="You approve each result" runs-in="Before anything goes out" what-happens="A named person reviews every result with the checklist beside the source material and any item marked insufficient evidence, one case at a time, and approves it, changes it or sends it back. No batch approval." why-its-here="Autonomy starts at level 2. You explicitly require approval before release or action. High volume does not waive that requirement." what-it-passes-on="Approved results only. Rejected ones go back with a note, and become test examples." next="approved: step 7, Result is ready" rules="AU1: if Starting point, then Plain automation starts at level 4, an AI workflow at level 3, and any agent at level 2. Autonomy is earned as the system proves itself.&#10;AU11: if Every result explicitly requires approval, then Cap autonomy at level 2 regardless of volume or checkability."><mxCell style="shape=parallelogram;perimeter=parallelogramPerimeter;fixedSize=1;size=16;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#13201b;spacing=8;fillColor=#fde4e1;strokeColor=#cf4a42;strokeWidth=2;dashed=1;" vertex="1" parent="recommended-layer"><mxGeometry x="980" y="245" width="200" height="110" as="geometry"/></mxCell></UserObject><UserObject id="recommended-end" label="&lt;b&gt;7. Result is ready&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px&quot;&gt;Finish · Delivered output&lt;/font&gt;" tooltip="What happens: The finished result is delivered to whoever needs it.&#10;&#10;Why it's here: This is the outcome the task exists to produce. Every run, and every failure, should be logged so you can review it.&#10;&#10;Passes on: Nothing further. Logged results become new test examples over time." step="7" kind="Finish" name="Result is ready" runs-in="Delivered output" what-happens="The finished result is delivered to whoever needs it." why-its-here="This is the outcome the task exists to produce. Every run, and every failure, should be logged so you can review it." what-it-passes-on="Nothing further. Logged results become new test examples over time." rules="AU9: if Always, then List when a person must step in: after repeated failures, and before any high-risk action."><mxCell style="rounded=1;arcSize=50;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#13201b;spacing=8;fillColor=#1c6650;strokeColor=#1c6650;fontColor=#ffffff;" vertex="1" parent="recommended-layer"><mxGeometry x="1290" y="330" width="200" height="110" as="geometry"/></mxCell></UserObject><mxCell id="recommended-e0" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=10;fontColor=#4d5b55;strokeColor=#7f8d87;endArrow=block;endFill=1;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" edge="1" parent="recommended-layer" source="recommended-start" target="recommended-router"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="recommended-e1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=10;fontColor=#4d5b55;strokeColor=#7f8d87;endArrow=block;endFill=1;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="recommended-layer" source="recommended-router" target="recommended-typeA"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="620" y="385"/><mxPoint x="620" y="215"/></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="recommended-e2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=10;fontColor=#4d5b55;strokeColor=#7f8d87;endArrow=block;endFill=1;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" edge="1" parent="recommended-layer" source="recommended-router" target="recommended-typeB"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="recommended-e3" value="not sure" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=10;fontColor=#4d5b55;strokeColor=#7f8d87;endArrow=block;endFill=1;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="recommended-layer" source="recommended-router" target="recommended-unclear"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="620" y="385"/><mxPoint x="620" y="555"/></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="recommended-e4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=10;fontColor=#4d5b55;strokeColor=#7f8d87;endArrow=block;endFill=1;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="recommended-layer" source="recommended-typeA" target="recommended-approve"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="925" y="215"/><mxPoint x="925" y="300"/></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="recommended-e5" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=10;fontColor=#4d5b55;strokeColor=#7f8d87;endArrow=block;endFill=1;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="recommended-layer" source="recommended-typeB" target="recommended-approve"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="925" y="385"/><mxPoint x="925" y="300"/></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="recommended-e6" value="approved" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=10;fontColor=#4d5b55;strokeColor=#7f8d87;endArrow=block;endFill=1;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="recommended-layer" source="recommended-approve" target="recommended-end"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="1235" y="300"/><mxPoint x="1235" y="385"/></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="recommended-e7" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=10;fontColor=#4d5b55;strokeColor=#7f8d87;endArrow=block;endFill=1;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" edge="1" parent="recommended-layer" source="recommended-unclear" target="recommended-end"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="recommended-c2" value="ONE PATH PER TYPE" style="text;html=1;align=center;fontSize=10;fontColor=#7f8d87;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="recommended-layer"><mxGeometry x="660" y="132" width="220" height="20" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="recommended-title" value="&lt;b style=&quot;font-size:20px&quot;&gt;Prepare draft Form 1040-SR returns with source provenance for human review&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#4d5b55&quot;&gt;An automated workflow with AI steps. No agent needed. · From the guide's rules&lt;/font&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=13;fontColor=#13201b;" vertex="1" parent="recommended-layer"><mxGeometry x="40" y="20" width="900" height="50" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="recommended-key-start" value="Start / finish" style="rounded=1;arcSize=50;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#13201b;spacing=8;fillColor=#1c6650;strokeColor=#1c6650;fontColor=#ffffff;" vertex="1" parent="recommended-layer"><mxGeometry x="40" y="82" width="135" height="34" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="recommended-key-decision" value="Decision" style="rhombus;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#13201b;spacing=8;fillColor=#fff6d6;strokeColor=#cfa52c;" vertex="1" parent="recommended-layer"><mxGeometry x="190" y="82" width="135" height="34" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="recommended-key-ai" value="AI step" style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#13201b;spacing=8;fillColor=#fdebd2;strokeColor=#e0802a;" vertex="1" parent="recommended-layer"><mxGeometry x="340" y="82" width="135" height="34" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="recommended-key-human" value="Person" style="shape=parallelogram;perimeter=parallelogramPerimeter;fixedSize=1;size=16;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#13201b;spacing=8;fillColor=#fde4e1;strokeColor=#cf4a42;dashed=1;" vertex="1" parent="recommended-layer"><mxGeometry x="490" y="82" width="135" height="34" as="geometry"/></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram><diagram id="simpler" name="Simpler start"><mxGraphModel grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="0" pageScale="1" math="0" shadow="0"><root><mxCell id="simpler-root"/><mxCell id="simpler-layer" parent="simpler-root"/><UserObject id="simpler-start" label="&lt;b&gt;1. You paste in an example&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px&quot;&gt;Trigger · Claude, by hand&lt;/font&gt;" tooltip="What happens: Work starts the way it does today.&#10;&#10;Why it's here: You said you'll start it yourself.&#10;&#10;Passes on: The item to work on." step="1" kind="Start" name="You paste in an example" runs-in="Claude, by hand" model-or-method="Manual start" how-it-works="Runs only when a person starts it." what-happens="Work starts the way it does today." why-its-here="You said you'll start it yourself." what-it-passes-on="The item to work on." next="step 2, One well-written prompt"><mxCell style="rounded=1;arcSize=50;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#13201b;spacing=8;fillColor=#1c6650;strokeColor=#1c6650;fontColor=#ffffff;" vertex="1" parent="simpler-layer"><mxGeometry x="50" y="160" width="200" height="110" as="geometry"/></mxCell></UserObject><UserObject id="simpler-prompt" label="&lt;b&gt;2. One well-written prompt&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px&quot;&gt;AI · Claude, examples attached · Sonnet 5.5&lt;/font&gt;" tooltip="What happens: A single prompt with good examples attached does the whole job in one go.&#10;&#10;Why it's here: A single prompt is often enough, and its failures show you exactly which step needs its own treatment.&#10;&#10;Passes on: A draft for you to check." step="2" kind="AI step" name="One well-written prompt" runs-in="Claude, examples attached" model-or-method="Claude Sonnet 5.5" why-this-model="A balanced model handles most judgement steps well at a reasonable cost per run." how-to-start="Build the first version on Claude Opus 5.5. Switch to Claude Sonnet 5.5 once it matches that baseline on your test examples. If Claude Opus 5.5 itself falls short on the hardest steps, try Claude Fable 5.1; it requires Anthropic to keep data for 30 days, so it is unavailable under zero data retention." alternative="Open-weight alternative: for example Kimi K2.6, GLM-5 or DeepSeek-V4-Pro (leading open-weight models in October 2026)." what-happens="A single prompt with good examples attached does the whole job in one go." why-its-here="A single prompt is often enough, and its failures show you exactly which step needs its own treatment." what-it-passes-on="A draft for you to check." next="step 3, You check the result" rules="S4: if AI workflow you start yourself, then Start with one well-written prompt and no extra tools."><mxCell style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#13201b;spacing=8;fillColor=#fdebd2;strokeColor=#e0802a;strokeWidth=2;" vertex="1" parent="simpler-layer"><mxGeometry x="360" y="160" width="200" height="110" as="geometry"/></mxCell></UserObject><UserObject id="simpler-approve" label="&lt;b&gt;3. You check the result&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px&quot;&gt;Person · Person&lt;/font&gt;" tooltip="What happens: You compare the draft with what good looks like, and note what the instructions need to say.&#10;&#10;Why it's here: This teaches you what to automate before you pay to automate it.&#10;&#10;Passes on: Approved results." step="3" kind="Person" name="You check the result" runs-in="Person" what-happens="You compare the draft with what good looks like, and note what the instructions need to say." why-its-here="This teaches you what to automate before you pay to automate it." what-it-passes-on="Approved results." next="step 4, Result is ready" rules="S4: if AI workflow you start yourself, then Start with one well-written prompt and no extra tools."><mxCell style="shape=parallelogram;perimeter=parallelogramPerimeter;fixedSize=1;size=16;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#13201b;spacing=8;fillColor=#fde4e1;strokeColor=#cf4a42;strokeWidth=2;dashed=1;" vertex="1" parent="simpler-layer"><mxGeometry x="670" y="160" width="200" height="110" as="geometry"/></mxCell></UserObject><UserObject id="simpler-end" label="&lt;b&gt;4. Result is ready&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px&quot;&gt;Finish · Delivered output&lt;/font&gt;" tooltip="What happens: The result goes out, exactly as it would in the full design.&#10;&#10;Why it's here: The outcome doesn't change; only how much is automated.&#10;&#10;Passes on: Nothing further. Note what went wrong: it shapes the full design." step="4" kind="Finish" name="Result is ready" runs-in="Delivered output" what-happens="The result goes out, exactly as it would in the full design." why-its-here="The outcome doesn't change; only how much is automated." what-it-passes-on="Nothing further. Note what went wrong: it shapes the full design."><mxCell style="rounded=1;arcSize=50;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#13201b;spacing=8;fillColor=#1c6650;strokeColor=#1c6650;fontColor=#ffffff;" vertex="1" parent="simpler-layer"><mxGeometry x="980" y="160" width="200" height="110" as="geometry"/></mxCell></UserObject><mxCell id="simp